Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc, libncurses-dev, pkgconf
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: netcfgd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: network configuration daemon that states what it will do
 netcfgd reads one declarative configuration, reports what the machine
 currently looks like, and prints the exact list of operations that would
 make one match the other. Applying is a separate step, and the plan is the
 thing an operator reviews.
 .
 It links no D-Bus, no polkit and no glib, and depends on no system message
 bus. The daemon speaks a newline-delimited JSON protocol over a unix socket.
 .
 Installing this package configures nothing and starts nothing. The systemd
 unit is installed and left disabled: netcfgd takes over an interface only
 when a configuration names it and an operator applies a plan.
